---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — File Tunnel"
  description="How the File Tunnel website and transfer system minimize retained data."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Less data, fewer surprises.</h1>
    <p class="lede">This marketing site has no cookies, analytics, forms, or third-party runtime scripts.</p>

    <h2>The transfer product</h2>
    <p>
      File Tunnel is designed for temporary transfer. A host application creates
      a short-lived tunnel, the sending device uploads selected files, and the
      receiving application imports them. Tunnel metadata and objects are
      scheduled for deletion at completion or expiry.
    </p>

    <h2>What must never enter telemetry</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>File content or thumbnails</li>
      <li>Pairing URLs, capabilities, or event tickets</li>
      <li>Local file paths or device handles</li>
      <li>User-entered filenames unless a host application explicitly owns that policy</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Host applications</h2>
    <p>
      File Tunnel is an embeddable platform. The application receiving a file
      decides what happens after import and should disclose its own retention
      and privacy practices.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
